int32_t gpuidx;
gpuidx = kfd_process_gpuidx_from_gpuid(ctx.process, prange->actual_loc);
if (gpuidx < 0) {
```
Reason:
By changing the type of `gpuidx` from `uint32_t` to `int32_t`, the variable can now correctly represent negative values returned by the function `kfd_process_gpuidx_from_gpuid`. This allows the comparison `if (gpuidx < 0)` to function as intended, enabling the code to handle error conditions properly.

